          "answer": 1,
          "solution": "The gold reserve held by the Reserve Bank of India serves as an asset to help balance payments in the Balance of Payments, especially during times of currency fluctuation or external debt pressure. It is not used for direct lending to banks (Option A), funding budget deficits directly (Option C), or farmer loans (Option D). These functions are handled through other mechanisms like foreign exchange reserves or government bonds. Thus, balancing payments is the correct primary function.",
